  "id": "Compound::DB06705 - Gene::213",
  "verbalization": "Gadofosveset Trisodium is implicated in the interaction with Alb through a shared pathway involving Sodium Lauryl Sulfate. The evidence suggests that Gadofosveset Trisodium causes various adverse effects, including Numbness Generalized, Mucosal Bleeding, and Mucosal Haemorrhage, all of which are mediated by Sodium Lauryl Sulfate. This sulfate compound then binds to Alb, establishing a potential mechanism by which Gadofosveset Trisodium may influence Alb's activity. The lowest common ancestor of these interactions is Sodium Lauryl Sulfate, reinforcing the link between the drug and Alb. The consistent presence of Sodium Lauryl Sulfate as a mediator across multiple pathways supports a unified mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction between Gadofosveset Trisodium and Alb remains to be fully elucidated.",
